@ 10.3.8 - Proto-Oceanic to Tolomako
# citation: thetha, from Lynch, John (2005), “The Apicolabial Shift in Nese”. Oceanic Linguistics 44(2):389 – 403; and http://language.psy.auckland.ac.nz/austronesian/
	C → ∅ / _#
	q → ∅
	*R → {∅,r} (the former seems more common)
	ɲ c *j → n s z
	m b → n̼ t̼ → n t / _{a,e,i}
	p(ʷ) k → v(ʷ) ɣ
	mʷ b(ʷ) vʷ → m p b
	d ɡ → r k
	{z,dr} → ts
	u → i (“sporadic”)
	a → e (rare?)